@@ -1,5 +1,20 @@
 # rusix progress
 
+The teardown KUnit archive gate now requires exactly one native fixture only in
+the explicit `exit-mmap-kunit-v1` context; ordinary profiles still reject it.
+This corrects the tooling rejection of retained matrix 001 after its ordinary
+C/Rust nine-case checks passed. The original KUnit attempt remains failed before
+VM execution. The first retained-object reinspection passed the archive check, then rejected
+the canonical Rust terminator: NORMAL speed is 3, not zero. The metadata gate now
+binds the native/generated enums and exact Rust constructor, requiring only that
+known speed field to be nonzero. All 32 host suites (338 cases) pass on 4,034
+stable inputs; production
+source is unchanged. The second read-only retained-object reinspection is prepared but not run; the
+first failure is retained, and a fresh paired KUnit retry remains required before
+downstream acceptance. The same zero-sentinel assumption is a known blocker in
+the separate PFN checker; its old draft must remain disabled pending a separately
+reviewed propagation.
+
 The inherited lifecycle verifier now accepts the observed private-cache `.0`
 suffix and proves the canonical refcount constant's four-byte storage/value.
 This carries the reviewed fix from `e0632d2729` without changing kernel code.
